[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. Now I have all the information needed to provide a comprehensive analysis. Let me compile the report:\n\n## COMPREHENSIVE ANALYSIS: Kynetic Spec Codebase\n\n### PROJECT OVERVIEW\n\n**Kynetic Spec (kspec)** is a **self-hosting specification and task management system** that manages what should be built and tracks progress on building it. The project uses itself to build itself—the spec files define kspec behavior, and the TypeScript code implements them.\n\n**Key Insight**: When agents work on this project, they ARE using kspec to build kspec.\n\n---\n\n### DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n\n```\n/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/\n├── .kspec/                           # Shadow branch worktree (orphan branch: kspec-meta)\n│   ├── kynetic.meta.yaml            # 612 top-level items (agents, workflows, conventions, etc.)\n│   ├── kynetic.yaml                 # Root manifest\n│   ├── project.tasks.yaml           # Active project tasks\n│   ├── project.inbox.yaml           # Inbox items\n│   ├── modules/                     # Spec items by domain\n│   ├── skills/                      # Project/local skills\n│   └── artifacts/                   # Task artifacts\n├── src/\n│   ├── cli/commands/\n│   │   ├── ralph.ts                 # Ralph loop orchestration (auto-agent runner)\n│   │   ├── agent.ts                 # Agent management commands\n│   │   ├── agents.ts                # Legacy agent generation (being replaced)\n│   │   ├── setup.ts                 # Setup pipeline for agent environment\n│   │   └── session.ts               # Session lifecycle management\n│   ├── agent-runtime/\n│   │   ├── dispatch.ts              # Core dispatch engine (state-change matching, queuing)\n│   │   ├── invocation.ts            # Invocation lifecycle\n│   │   └── prompts.ts               # Prompt building\n│   ├── ralph/                       # Ralph automation framework (2,237 lines)\n│   │   ├── cli-renderer.ts          # CLI output formatting\n│   │   ├── events.ts                # Event translation & session recording\n│   │   ├── index.ts                 # Core exports\n│   │   ├── loop-errors.ts           # Loop error handling\n│   │   ├── subagent.ts              # Subagent spawning\n│   │   └── wrap-up.ts               # Wrap-up agent logic\n│   ├── agents/\n│   │   ├── adapters.ts              # ACP adapter registry\n│   │   ├── spawner.ts               # Agent spawning\n│   │   └── index.ts                 # Exports\n│   ├── parser/\n│   │   ├── meta.ts                  # Meta context loading\n│   │   ├── agent-detection.ts       # Auto-detect agent environment\n│   │   ├── skill-render.ts          # Skill rendering to multiple platforms\n│   │   └── shadow.ts                # Shadow branch worktree management\n│   ├── schema/\n│   │   └── meta.ts                  # Zod schemas (Agent, Workflow, Convention, etc.)\n│   └── sessions/\n│       └── *.ts                     # Session event storage & budget tracking\n├── templates/\n│   ├── agents-sections/             # Static markdown sections for kspec-agents.md\n│   │   ├── 06-ralph-loop.md        # Ralph loop documentation\n│   │   └── *.md                     # Other sections\n│   └── skills/\n│       ├── manifest.yaml            # Core skills listing\n│       ├── task-work/SKILL.md       # Structured task lifecycle skill\n│       ├── reflect/SKILL.md         # Reflection skill\n│       ├── local-review/SKILL.md    # Pre-PR review skill\n│       └── ... (14 total core skills)\n├── tests/\n│   ├── ralph.test.ts                # Ralph loop tests (2,845 lines)\n│   ├── ralph-wrap-up.test.ts        # Wrap-up subagent tests (474 lines)\n│   ├── ralph-context-refresh.test.ts # Context refresh tests (579 lines)\n│   ├── ralph-loop-errors.test.ts    # Error handling tests (518 lines)\n│   ├── agent-dispatch-engine.test.ts # Dispatch engine tests\n│   ├── cli-agent-commands.test.ts   # CLI agent command tests\n│   └── helpers/cli.ts               # Test helpers (setupTempFixtures, kspec, etc.)\n├── packages/web-ui/                 # SvelteKit daemon web interface\n└── dist/                            # Compiled output\n```\n\n---\n\n### 1. SCHEMA DEFINITIONS (Source of Truth)\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/schema/meta.ts`\n\nThe Zod schemas define the structure and validation for all meta items:\n\n#### Agent Definition Schema\n```typescript\nexport const AgentSchema = z.object({\n  _ulid: MetaUlidSchema,                    // Unique ID\n  id: z.string(),                           // Human-friendly identifier\n  name: z.string(),                         // Display name\n  description: z.string().optional(),       // What this agent does\n  capabilities: z.array(z.string()),        // [code, test, review, etc.]\n  tools: z.array(z.string()),               // [kspec, git, npm, etc.]\n  session_protocol: SessionProtocolSchema,  // start/checkpoint/end commands\n  conventions: z.array(z.string()),         // Behavioral rules\n  \n  // ← NEW RUNTIME/DISPATCH FIELDS (AC: @agent-definition-schema ac-1 through ac-8)\n  adapter: z.string().optional(),           // ACP adapter ID (e.g., \"claude-agent-acp\")\n  dispatch: z.array(AgentDispatchRuleSchema).default([]),  // Trigger rules\n  skills: z.array(z.string()).default([]),  // Attached skills\n  budget: AgentBudgetSchema.optional(),     // max_tasks, timeout_minutes\n  concurrency: AgentConcurrencySchema,      // max_concurrent workers\n  auto_approve: z.boolean(),                // Auto-approve certain actions\n  prompt_template: z.string().optional(),   // Custom prompt override\n  automation: z.enum([\"eligible\", \"ineligible\"]).optional(),  // Filtering\n  tags: z.array(z.string()).optional(),     // Categorization\n});\n```\n\n#### Agent Dispatch Event Types\n```typescript\nexport const AgentDispatchEventSchema = z.enum([\n  \"task.ready\",         // Task moved to pending (ready to start)\n  \"task.needs_work\",    // Task marked needs_work (review feedback)\n  \"task.pending_review\" // Task marked pending_review (needs review)\n]);\n```\n\n#### Agent Dispatch Rule (Matches Event → Optional Filters)\n```typescript\nexport const AgentDispatchRuleSchema = z.object({\n  on: AgentDispatchEventSchema,       // Which event triggers this\n  filter: AgentDispatchFilterSchema.optional()  // Constraints:\n    // - automation: eligible|ineligible\n    // - tags: [array of required tags]\n    // - priority: minimum priority level\n});\n```\n\n#### Agent Budget Schema\n```typescript\nexport const AgentBudgetSchema = z.object({\n  max_tasks: z.number().positive().optional(),      // Task limit per session\n  timeout_minutes: z.number().positive().optional() // Session timeout\n});\n```\n\n#### Agent Concurrency Schema\n```typescript\nexport const AgentConcurrencySchema = z.object({\n  max_concurrent: z.number().int().positive().default(1) // Parallel workers allowed\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. AGENT DEFINITIONS (Runtime Instance)\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml` (lines 1-70)\n\nCurrent agents in the system:\n\n```yaml\nagents:\n  - _ulid: 01KF782ZSF5ZQTN2PKZPH6ASKA\n    id: claude\n    name: Claude Code Agent\n    description: |\n      Primary AI development agent for kynetic-spec.\n      Works via Claude Code CLI in terminal sessions.\n    capabilities:\n      - code\n      - test\n      - refactor\n      - review\n      - design\n      - document\n    tools:\n      - kspec\n      - git\n      - npm\n      - vitest\n    session_protocol:\n      start: kspec session start\n      checkpoint: kspec session checkpoint\n    conventions:\n      - Always use kspec CLI, never edit YAML directly\n      - Add notes when completing significant work\n      - Check spec coverage before implementing behavior changes\n      - Commit changes before ending session\n    dispatch: []  # No automatic dispatch rules yet\n    skills: []    # No skills attached\n    concurrency:\n      max_concurrent: 1\n    auto_approve: false\n\n  # Additional test agents (json-test, json-test2, automation-assess)\n```\n\n**Key Observations**:\n- Agents are defined in `.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml` (shadow branch state)\n- The `claude` agent has **no dispatch rules** (dispatch is empty)\n- The `claude` agent has **no attached skills** (skills array is empty)\n- No adapters specified (would need to reference ACP adapter IDs)\n\n---\n\n### 3. DISPATCH ENGINE (Runtime Matching)\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/agent-runtime/dispatch.ts` (149 lines shown)\n\nThe **DispatchEngine** watches for task state changes and matches them against agent dispatch rules.\n\n#### Core Mapping\n```typescript\n// Task status → Dispatch event mapping\nconst EVENT_TO_STATUS: Record<string, TaskStatus> = {\n  \"task.ready\": \"pending\",         // → Task in pending status\n  \"task.needs_work\": \"needs_work\", // → Task in needs_work status\n  \"task.pending_review\": \"pending_review\" // → Task in pending_review\n};\n\nconst STATUS_TO_EVENT: Record<TaskStatus, string | undefined> = {\n  pending: \"task.ready\",\n  needs_work: \"task.needs_work\",\n  pending_review: \"task.pending_review\",\n  in_progress: undefined,          // No trigger for in_progress\n  blocked: undefined,\n  completed: undefined,\n  cancelled: undefined,\n};\n```\n\n#### Task State Change Event\n```typescript\nexport interface TaskStateChange {\n  taskId: string;                   // ULID\n  taskRef: string;                  // slug (e.g., \"test-task-pending\")\n  fromStatus: TaskStatus;\n  toStatus: TaskStatus;\n  timestamp: number;\n  task?: LoadedTask;                // Actual task data for filter evaluation\n}\n```\n\n#### Queue Entry Structure\n```typescript\ninterface QueueEntry {\n  agent: LoadedAgent;\n  change: TaskStateChange;\n  retryCount: number;\n  nextRetryAt: number;\n  enqueuedAtMs: number;             // For wait-time tracking\n}\n```\n\n#### Key Responsibilities\n- **Watch file changes**: Monitors `.kspec/project.tasks.yaml` for state changes\n- **Match dispatch rules**: When task status changes, find agents with matching `dispatch.on` events\n- **Filter evaluation**: Apply filters (automation=eligible, tags, priority)\n- **Queue management**: Hold queued invocations with deduplication & retry logic\n- **Concurrency control**: Respect `agent.concurrency.max_concurrent` limits\n- **Serialization**: Use mutex to serialize shadow branch mutations when multiple agents run\n\n---\n\n### 4. AGENT DISPATCH COMMAND\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/agent.ts` (150+ lines shown)\n\nProvides CLI commands for agent management:\n\n#### `kspec agent list`\n```bash\nkspec agent list [--json] [--status eligible|ineligible] [--tag TAG] [--limit N] [--offset N] [--count]\n```\n- Lists all agents defined in meta\n- Filters by automation status, tags, priority\n- Supports pagination (limit/offset)\n- Count mode for querying total\n\n#### `kspec agent run`\n- Run a one-off agent invocation with custom options\n- Not for automated dispatch (that's the daemon's job)\n\n#### `kspec agent status`\n- Query daemon dispatch engine state\n- Shows running invocations, queued tasks, active agents\n- **AC: @cli-agent-commands ac-10** - Get daemon URL from PID file\n\n---\n\n### 5. ADAPTER REGISTRY (ACP Client Binding)\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/agents/adapters.ts`\n\n```typescript\nexport interface AgentAdapter {\n  command: string;                  // Executable (e.g., \"node\", \"codex\")\n  args: string[];                   // Base arguments\n  env?: Record<string, string>;     // Environment variables\n  description: string;              // Human-readable description\n}\n\n// Registry management\nexport function registerAdapter(id: string, adapter: AgentAdapter): void;\nexport function resolveAdapter(id?: string): AgentAdapter;  // Default: claude-agent-acp\n```\n\n**Registered Adapters**:\n- `claude-agent-acp` (default) — Claude agent via ACP protocol\n- `codex-acp` — Codex CLI via ACP\n- `custom` — Custom command (via ralph --adapter-cmd)\n\n---\n\n### 6. RALPH AUTOMATION FRAMEWORK\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` (1,600+ lines)\n\nRalph is the **autonomous loop orchestrator**. It runs an ACP-compliant agent in a loop to process tasks automatically.\n\n#### Core Command\n```bash\nkspec ralph [--max-loops N] [--restart-every N] [--adapter-cmd COMMAND] [--dry-run] ...\n```\n\n#### Ralph Loop Architecture\n\n```\nralph command\n  ↓\nInitialize session context (get ready tasks, meta, skills)\n  ↓\nFOR each iteration (1..maxLoops):\n  1. Check for automation-eligible tasks (ready or in_progress)\n  2. IF none → EXIT\n  3. Build worker prompt + skill invocations\n     - Includes: /kspec:task-work loop\n     - Includes: /kspec:reflect loop\n  4. Spawn worker agent (via adapter_cmd)\n  5. ON agent completion:\n     a. Process pending_review tasks via subagent (review skill)\n     b. Run reflection subagent\n  6. ON failure:\n     - Retry (up to max_retries)\n     - Track per-task failures\n     - Escalate at threshold (3 consecutive failures)\n  7. Continue to next iteration\n  ↓\nWrap up (final reflection, session cleanup)\n```\n\n#### Skill Delegation Pattern\nRalph does **NOT parse or invoke skills**—it embeds skill invocations in prompts:\n\n```typescript\n// AC: @ralph-skill-delegation ac-3\n// Skills are embedded as text, not parsed/executed by Ralph\nconst workerTaskWorkSkill = resolveRalphSkillInvocation(\n  ctx.config.ralph.skills.task_work,  // e.g., \"/kspec:task-work\"\n  workerPromptPlatform,\n  skillOrigins,\n);\n\n// In prompt:\nconst prompt = `\n## Task Work\nWhen ready, run the following skill:\n${workerTaskWorkSkill} loop\n\nThis skill manages the complete task lifecycle...\n`;\n```\n\n**Key Functions** (exported from src/cli/commands/ralph.ts):\n- `createSessionUpdateLogger()` — Session event recording\n- `disposeSpawnedAgent()` — Clean up spawned processes\n- `getPromptPlatformForAdapter()` — Detect platform (claude-code, codex, unknown)\n- `pushRecentTaskRef()` — Track task history for hints\n- `resolveRalphSkillInvocation()` — Normalize skill invocation strings\n- `runTerminalCommandWithArtifacts()` — Execute terminal commands in session\n\n---\n\n### 7. RALPH MODULES (Supporting Ralph)\n\n**Ralph Framework** (`/src/ralph/`, 2,237 total lines):\n\n| Module | Lines | Purpose |\n|--------|-------|---------|\n| `events.ts` | 799 | Event translation, session recording, state dumps |\n| `subagent.ts` | 424 | Spawn subagents for PR review, reflection |\n| `wrap-up.ts` | 398 | Final wrap-up agent & session cleanup |\n| `loop-errors.ts` | 198 | Error tracking, failure escalation |\n| `cli-renderer.ts` | 347 | Format iteration output, prompts for display |\n| `index.ts` | 71 | Core exports & constants |\n\n#### Key Exports from `/src/ralph/index.ts`:\n- `createTranslator()` — SessionUpdate → Event translator\n- `createCliRenderer()` — Format prompt sections\n- `buildWrapUpContext()` — Prepare wrap-up state\n- `runSubagent()`, `runWrapUpAgent()` — Subagent execution\n- `DEFAULT_SUBAGENT_PREFIX` = \"ralph\"\n- `DEFAULT_WRAPUP_TIMEOUT` = 600000ms (10 min)\n- `RALPH_PROMPT_TIMEOUT` = 1200000ms (20 min)\n- `WORKER_PROMPT_MAX_BYTES` = 200KB (budget for worker prompt)\n\n---\n\n### 8. WORKFLOWS (Process Definitions)\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml` (lines 71+, 612 total items)\n\nWorkflows define structured processes. Key examples:\n\n```yaml\nworkflows:\n  - _ulid: 01KF782ZSH8JG4CCJRWVQQ9G5R\n    id: spec-first\n    trigger: behavior-change\n    description: Check spec coverage before implementing changes...\n    steps: [...]\n\n  - _ulid: 01KFM9SNV2QRRGREJ1HMZWXCFT\n    id: task-work-loop\n    trigger: manual\n    description: Loop variant of task-work-session for autonomous agents...\n    steps: [...]  # Detailed steps for autonomous execution\n\n  - _ulid: ...\n    id: session-reflect-loop\n    trigger: loop-iteration-end\n    description: Autonomous reflection for loop mode...\n```\n\n**Workflow Types**:\n- **Manual** (task-work-session, spec-plan-design) — Human-initiated\n- **Automated** (task-work-loop, session-reflect-loop) — Ralph loop-triggered\n- **Process** (pr-review-merge, spec-first) — Guides behavior\n\n**Workflow Step Types**:\n```typescript\nexport const WorkflowStepTypeSchema = z.enum([\"check\", \"action\", \"decision\"]);\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. SKILLS (Reusable Capabilities)\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/templates/skills/manifest.yaml` (14 core skills)\n\nSkills are reusable components that agents can invoke. They're authored in `templates/skills/` and rendered to multiple platforms.\n\n#### Core Skills:\n| ID | Name | Platforms | Purpose |\n|----|------|-----------|---------|\n| `help` | Kspec Help | claude-code, codex | CLI reference |\n| `task-work` | Task Work | claude-code, codex | Task lifecycle |\n| `reflect` | Session Reflection | claude-code, codex | End-of-session reflection |\n| `triage` | Triage | claude-code, codex | Inbox + observation triage |\n| `triage-inbox` | Inbox Triage | claude-code, codex | Item categorization |\n| `triage-automation` | Automation Triage | claude-code, codex | Assess automation readiness |\n| `writing-specs` | Writing Specs | claude-code, codex | Spec creation |\n| `plan` | Plan to Spec | claude-code, codex | Plan translation |\n| `create-workflow` | Create Workflow | claude-code, codex | Workflow formalization |\n| `review` | Review | claude-code, codex | Review gates (AC coverage, etc.) |\n| `audit` | Codebase Audit | claude-code, codex | Release readiness |\n| `codex` | Codex CLI | claude-code, codex | Delegate to GPT-5.3 |\n| `e2e` | E2E Testing | claude-code, codex | Playwright test patterns |\n| `eval-agents` | Eval Agents | claude-code, codex | AGENTS.md validation |\n| `local-review` | Pre-PR Review | claude-code, codex | Quality gates |\n| ... (project skills in `.kspec/skills/`) | ... | ... | ... |\n\n#### Skill Platforms:\n- `claude-code` — Claude Code CLI (rendered to `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md`)\n- `codex` — Codex CLI (rendered format TBD)\n- `aider` — Aider CLI (if registered)\n\n#### Skill Rendering:\n```typescript\n// From src/parser/skill-render.ts\nexport function getRenderer(platform: string): SkillRenderer | null;\nexport function resolveSkillReferenceTokensForPlatform(\n  invocation: string,\n  platform: RalphPromptPlatform,\n  skillOrigins: Map<string, SkillOrigin>,\n): string;\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10. SETUP PIPELINE (Agent Environment)\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/setup.ts` (1,600+ lines)\n\nThe **setup command** orchestrates full onboarding:\n\n```bash\nkspec setup [--agent TYPE] [--dry-run] [--status] [--force]\n```\n\n#### Pipeline Steps:\n1. **Agent Detection** — Detect environment (Claude Code, Cline, Codex, etc.)\n2. **Install Core Skills** — Copy core skills to `.kspec/skills/`\n3. **Register Plugin Marketplace** — (Claude Code only)\n4. **Install Hooks** — Claude Code hooks:\n   - `UserPromptSubmit` → `kspec session prompt-check`\n   - `Stop` → `kspec session checkpoint --json`\n   - `PreToolUse` → `kspec guard worktree` (native guard command)\n5. **Create Artifacts Directory** — `.kspec/artifacts/`\n6. **Seed Permissions** — Claude Code `~/.claude/settings.json`\n7. **Seed Memory** — Platform-specific memory (Claude Code, etc.)\n8. **Render Skills** — For each skill, call platform renderer\n9. **Generate kspec-agents.md** — Auto-generated agent instructions\n\n#### Setup Result:\n```typescript\nexport interface SetupPipelineResult {\n  success: boolean;\n  steps: SetupStepResult[];\n  coreSkillsInstalled: number;\n  skillsRendered: number;\n  hooksInstalled: boolean;\n  agentsMdGenerated: boolean;\n  permissionsSeeded: boolean;\n  memorySeeded: boolean;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 11. SESSION MANAGEMENT\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/session.ts`\n\nSessions track work context across commands.\n\n#### Session Context\n```typescript\nexport interface SessionStartContext {\n  activeTasksSummary: ActiveTaskSummary[];  // Current work\n  sessionId: string;                        // ULID\n  tasksReady: number;                       // Pending tasks\n  tasksInProgress: number;\n  tasksPendingReview: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ActiveTaskSummary {\n  ref: string;                              // Task slug\n  ulid: string;                             // ULID\n  title: string;\n  status: TaskStatus;\n  automation?: string;                      // eligible|ineligible|needs_review\n}\n```\n\n#### Session Lifecycle\n```bash\nkspec session start       # Get session context, show active work\nkspec session checkpoint --json  # Checkpoint at pause/stop\n```\n\n---\n\n### 12. RALPH TESTS\n\n**Files**:\n- `tests/ralph.test.ts` (2,845 lines) — Main loop tests\n- `tests/ralph-wrap-up.test.ts` (474 lines) — Wrap-up subagent\n- `tests/ralph-context-refresh.test.ts` (579 lines) — Context refresh\n- `tests/ralph-loop-errors.test.ts` (518 lines) — Error handling\n\n#### Test Pattern:\n```typescript\nfunction runRalph(\n  args: string,\n  cwd: string,\n  env: Record<string, string> = {}\n): RalphResult {\n  const result = spawnSync(\n    'node',\n    [CLI_PATH, 'ralph', ...args.split(/\\s+/), '--adapter-cmd', `node ${MOCK_ACP}`],\n    { cwd, encoding: 'utf-8', timeout: 30000, env: {...process.env, ...env}}\n  );\n  return { output: stdout + stderr, stdout, stderr, exitCode };\n}\n\n// AC: @cli-ralph ac-1 - Basic loop execution\nit('executes loop iterations when ready tasks exist', async () => {\n  const result = runRalph('--max-loops 2', tempDir, {MOCK_ACP_EXIT_CODE: '0'});\n  expect(result.stdout).toContain('Iteration 1/2');\n  expect(result.stdout).toContain('Iteration 2/2');\n  expect(result.stdout).toContain('Ralph loop completed');\n});\n```\n\n#### Test Coverage:\n- Loop execution (iterations, completion)\n- No-ready-tasks exit behavior\n- Automation-eligible task filtering\n- Dry-run mode output\n- Timeout handling & escalation\n- Failure retries & continuation\n- Skill delegation (no parsing/invocation)\n- Pending review task processing\n- Context refresh after review\n- Iteration timeout with event logging\n\n---\n\n### 13. AGENT DISPATCH ENGINE TESTS\n\n**File**: `tests/agent-dispatch-engine.test.ts`\n\nTests the dispatch engine core:\n- State change matching\n- Filter evaluation (automation, tags, priority)\n- Queue deduplication\n- Concurrency limits\n- Serialized mutations\n- Graceful shutdown\n\n---\n\n### 14. CLI AGENT COMMANDS TESTS\n\n**File**: `tests/cli-agent-commands.test.ts`\n\nTests agent command handlers:\n- `kspec agent list` (filtering, pagination)\n- `kspec agent run` (one-off invocation)\n- `kspec agent status` (daemon state)\n- Adapter resolution\n\n---\n\n### 15. KSPEC-AGENTS.MD (Auto-Generated Instructions)\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/kspec-agents.md` (auto-generated from agents.ts)\n\n**Source**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/agents.ts`\n\n#### Generation Process:\n```\nkspec agents generate\n  ↓\nLoad meta context (agents, workflows, conventions, skills)\n  ↓\nLoad template sections from templates/agents-sections/*.md\n  ↓\nGenerate content using:\n  - Agent info (capabilities, tools, conventions)\n  - Skill table with descriptions\n  - Convention rules with examples\n  - Workflow descriptions\n  - Template content (injected dynamically)\n  ↓\nWrite to kspec-agents.md\n  ↓\nStore meta hash for staleness detection\n```\n\n#### Content Structure:\n- Finding Information (skill table + CLI help)\n- Conventions (commits, notes, naming, tags, branching, documentation, testing)\n- Workflows (available workflows with trigger types)\n- Quick Start (kspec init, kspec session start)\n- Essential Rules (CLI over YAML, spec-first, notes, dependencies, etc.)\n- Shadow Branch Architecture (worktree explanation)\n- Task Lifecycle (states, spec-first development)\n- PR Workflow (local review → PR → merge)\n- Ralph Loop Mode (autonomous execution)\n- Batch Usage (multi-command atomic commits)\n\n---\n\n### 16. AGENT DETECTION\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/parser/agent-detection.ts`\n\nAuto-detect which agent environment is running:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface DetectionResult {\n  type: AgentType;          // claude-code | cline | roo-code | copilot-cli | etc.\n  confidence: \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"low\";\n  configPath?: string;      // Path to config file if applicable\n  envVars?: Record<string, string>;\n}\n\nexport function detectAgentFromEnv(): DetectionResult;\n```\n\n**Detection Priority**:\n1. Environment variables (specific markers per agent type)\n2. Config file presence (~/.claude/ for Claude Code)\n3. Fallback to \"unknown\"\n\n---\n\n### 17. SHADOW BRANCH ARCHITECTURE\n\n**Structure**: `.kspec/` is a **git worktree** on orphan branch `kspec-meta`\n\n```\n.kspec/.git → worktree pointer\n  ↓\n.git/worktrees/kspec-meta\n  ↓\nkspec-meta branch (orphan): contains YAML state files\n```\n\n**Why**: Spec/task changes don't clutter main branch history. Code PRs and spec changes tracked independently.\n\n**Commands**:\n```bash\nkspec shadow status   # Verify health\nkspec shadow repair   # Fix broken worktree\nkspec shadow sync     # Sync with remote\n```\n\n**Custom Merge Driver** (for YAML conflict resolution):\n```bash\ngit config merge.kspec.driver \"kspec merge-driver %O %A %B %P\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 18. AGENT INVOCATION LIFECYCLE\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/agent-runtime/invocation.ts`\n\n```typescript\nexport async function runInvocation(\n  agent: LoadedAgent,\n  options: InvocationOptions\n): Promise<InvocationResult>;\n\nexport interface InvocationOptions {\n  taskRef?: string;              // Task being worked on\n  force?: boolean;               // Override concurrency limits\n  noPrompt?: boolean;            // Skip prompt (testing)\n  env?: Record<string, string>;  // Extra environment\n  budget?: AgentBudget;          // Override agent budget\n}\n\nexport interface InvocationResult {\n  invocationId: string;          // ULID\n  success: boolean;\n  exitCode: number;\n  logs?: string;\n  durationMs: number;\n}\n```\n\n#### Invocation Flow:\n1. **Resolve Adapter** — Get command + args for agent\n2. **Build Prompt** — Include skills, task context, instructions\n3. **Spawn Process** — Execute adapter command with ACP protocol\n4. **Session Recording** — Log all SessionUpdate events\n5. **Budget Tracking** — Monitor task count, time\n6. **Cleanup** — Dispose process, finalize session\n\n---\n\n### 19. CONVENTIONS\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/kspec-agents.md` (extracted from meta)\n\nProject-enforced conventions:\n\n| Domain | Rules |\n|--------|-------|\n| **commits** | Conventional format (feat/fix/docs/etc), kebab-case, under 72 chars, Co-Authored-By for AI |\n| **notes** | Required when completing work, include what/why/approach |\n| **naming** | kebab-case for slugs, task- prefix, descriptive |\n| **tags** | Lowercase, max 3-5 per item, domain tags (cli, schema, etc.) |\n| **branching** | Descriptive branch names, prefixes (feat/, fix/), kebab-case |\n| **documentation** | Explain why, include examples, keep close to code |\n| **testing** | ULIDs via testUlid(), never JSON.stringify() for YAML, E2E separate |\n| **development** | node scripts/bootstrap.cjs, use kspec CLI, daemon on 3456 |\n| **ci** | File watcher tests skip, E2E hardcoded on 3456 |\n\n---\n\n### 20. TEST HELPERS\n\n**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/tests/helpers/cli.ts`\n\n```typescript\nexport async function setupTempFixtures(): Promise<string>;\nexport async function createTempDir(): Promise<string>;\nexport function initGitRepo(dir: string): void;\nexport function testUlid(prefix?: string): string;  // Deterministic test ULIDs\nexport function testUlids(prefix: string, count: number): string[];\nexport async function kspec(args: string, cwd: string): Promise<CliResult>;\nexport async function kspecJson<T>(args: string, cwd: string): Promise<T>;\nexport async function cleanupTempDir(dir: string): Promise<void>;\n```\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY: How Agents Fit Into Kynetic Spec\n\n### Design Pattern:\n\n```\n┌─ DEFINITION LAYER (Schema)\n│  └─ Agent = {id, name, capabilities, dispatch rules, skills, adapter, budget, concurrency}\n│\n├─ RUNTIME LAYER (Dispatch Engine)\n│  └─ Watch task state changes → Match against agent.dispatch rules → Queue invocations\n│\n├─ INVOCATION LAYER (Ralph / Manual)\n│  └─ Spawn agent via adapter (ACP protocol) → Run with skills → Record session\n│\n├─ AUTOMATION LAYER (Ralph Loop)\n│  └─ Orchestrate autonomous iterations: work → review → reflect\n│\n└─ DELIVERY LAYER (Setup)\n   └─ Detect environment → Install hooks → Render skills → Generate instructions\n```\n\n### Key Files & Line Counts:\n- **Schema** (`src/schema/meta.ts`): Agent structure definition\n- **Dispatch** (`src/agent-runtime/dispatch.ts`): State-change matching\n- **Ralph Command** (`src/cli/commands/ralph.ts`): Loop orchestration\n- **Ralph Framework** (`src/ralph/*.ts`): Supporting modules (2,237 lines)\n- **Setup** (`src/cli/commands/setup.ts`): Environment configuration (1,600+ lines)\n- **Tests** (`tests/ralph*.test.ts`, `tests/agent*.test.ts`): 4,416+ lines\n\n### Absolute File Paths (for reference):\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/schema/meta.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/agent-runtime/dispatch.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/ralph.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/agent.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/setup.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/agents.ts`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/kspec-agents.md`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/templates/agents-sections/06-ralph-loop.md`\n- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/templates/skills/manifest.yaml`\n\nThis comprehensive system enables **self-hosting automation**: agents are defined in meta, matched by the dispatch engine, spawned via adapters, and guided by skills—all while using kspec itself to manage the work."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ad7af3b (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 85844\ntool_uses: 43\nduration_ms: 122045</usage>"}]